[en.FOCUS_GEN_INDUSTRY_LOGS]
Cut!

[en.FOCUS_GEN_INDUSTRY_LOGS_desc]
A year 1 tree is typically small and fragile, with a thin trunk and a limited number of branches.\nA year 10 tree has experienced significant growth. The trunk is thicker and stronger, providing better structural support.\nA year 20 tree is mature and well-established. The trunk is thick and sturdy, and the branches are numerous and full of leaves.\nA year 30 tree is old and wise. The trunk is massive and the branches are heavy with foliage, providing ample shade and shelter.\nA year 40 tree is probably enthusiastic and warm, as it has been cut down and turned into firewood.

[zh.FOCUS_GEN_INDUSTRY_LOGS]
砍！

[zh.FOCUS_GEN_INDUSTRY_LOGS_desc]
一棵一年的树通常很小，很脆弱，树干细小，分支有限。\n一棵十年的树经历了显著的生长，树干更粗更结实，提供更好的结构支持。\n一棵二十年的树已经成熟并且根深蒂固，树干粗壮，分支众多，叶子繁茂。\n一棵三十年的树已经老而睿智，树干巨大，分支繁茂，叶子茂盛，提供了充足的阴凉和庇护。\n一棵四十年的树可能是热情而温暖的，因为它已经被砍伐并变成了柴火。

